---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { render, getCollection } from "astro:content";

const workExperience = await getCollection("workExperience");
---

<MainLayout
  title="Journal"
  description="A list of texts and articles I wrote over the years."
>
  <header>
    <h2>Resume</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Colleagues call me <em>a designer?</em> and <em>a developer?</em> – pronouncing
      the question mark on both. I design for screens most of the time, and I develop
      for the front-end when a project calls for it. My best work is done when I get
      to cover both the design and development roles.
    </p>
    <p>
      While I love a good marketing website, I usually fit best with work done
      on products with complex user interfaces, and when I can integrate into a
      small, competent product and development team.
    </p>
  </header>

  <h3 class="with-dotted-bg">Clients and workplaces</h3>
  <ul class="experience">
    {
      workExperience
        .sort((a, b) => b.data.timePeriod.localeCompare(a.data.timePeriod))
        .map(async (item) => {
          const { Content } = await render(item);
          return (
            <li class="work-item">
              <h4>{item.data.name}</h4>
              <p class="time-period">
                <strong>{item.data.timePeriod}</strong> /{" "}
                {item.data.responsibilities}
              </p>
              <div class="content">
                <Content />
              </div>
            </li>
          );
        })
    }
  </ul>

  <h3 class="with-dotted-bg">Relevant skills</h3>
  <ul class="skills">
    <li>
      <h4>0 → 1 product design</h4>
      <p>
        Working with small teams and founders, I’ve become very good at helping
        people go from <em>I have an idea</em> to <em
          >I know exactly what we’re going to do</em
        >. I treat design as the (fun, difficult) act of planning how to turn an
        idea and vision into something that’s ready to get implemented.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h4>User experience</h4>
      <p>
        I’ve been structuring apps since before <em>UX</em> became the <em
          >mot du jour</em
        > with leadership. My work involves defining user flows, auditing existing
        solutions. In particular, I make sure that whatever process gets moved to
        a digital equivalent actually improves on its current analog.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h4>Interface design</h4>
      <p>
        I make personality coexist with function. I build strong interfaces by
        making them visually clear, strong in their identity and branding, and
        by making sure they’re easy to use with the right mix of organization
        and visual cues.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h4>Front-of-the-front-end</h4>
      <p>
        I take part in developing the final interface. Usually, I’m at my best
        when I support a front-end team or person, and contribute with code that
        directly controls the appearance of the intercace. For small-scale web
        projects, I sometimes take charge of complete development.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="with-dotted-bg">Can we talk?</h3>
  <p>
    Of course! The best way to reach me is <a
      href="mailto:monsieur@louis-andre.net">by email</a
    >. I'm also on <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/louis-andre.net">Bluesky</a
    > and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/louis-andre-labadie">LinkedIn</a> if
    that's your preference.
  </p>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  header {
    max-width: 52rem;

    margin-bottom: 2rem;

    h2 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      font-family: var(--font-plex-condensed);
      margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
      margin-left: -0.025rem;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      max-width: 40em;
    }

    p.intro {
      font-weight: 350;
      font-size: 1.375rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
  }

  h3 {
    color: var(--mainAccent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin: 3rem -1rem 1rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  ul.experience {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;

    li {
      padding-top: 1rem;
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: auto;
      grid-template-areas:
        "a b"
        "c c";

      h4,
      .time-period {
        align-self: baseline;
        padding-bottom: 0;
        margin: 0;
      }

      h4 {
        font-family: var(--font-plex-condensed);
        font-weight: 300;
        font-size: 1.45rem;
        grid-area: a;
      }

      .time-period {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        color: var(--mainAccent);
        grid-area: b;
        align-self: baseline;
      }

      .content {
        border-top: solid 1px var(--fadedAccent);
        grid-area: c;
        padding-left: calc(50% + 0.5rem);
        font-size: 0.875rem;
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        padding-top: 2rem;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        grid-template-areas: "a" "b" "c";

        .content {
          padding: 0;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  ul.skills {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: auto;

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    h4 {
      color: var(--mainAccent);
      font-weight: 300;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      margin: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
